IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `qda-dates`
IMPORT `qda-core`
IMPORT `qda-admin`
IMPORT `qda-vehicles`

-- Duties Act 2001 (Queensland), with the Duties Regulation 2023 and the Taxation Administration Act 2001 as they apply to
-- duty -- the buyer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the buyer of a home, of residential vacant land, or of a vehicle: the transferee under the dutiable transaction,
-- or the person applying to register a vehicle or to have it transferred into their name. Every question is phrased as
-- that buyer asks it, on facts the buyer can state. The rules are in qda-core.l4 (transfer duty, home concessions,
-- clawback, AFAD, lodging), qda-admin.l4 (payment, interest, penalty tax, objections, appeals) and qda-vehicles.l4
-- (vehicle registration duty); this module builds their records from plain answers and restates no rule.
--
-- The home questions share one list of thirteen answers, in the same order, so the form asks them once; the question on
-- the transfer duty in all adds a fourteenth (whether the land is AFAD residential land), which matters only for a
-- foreign buyer. "Transfer duty" there is the Act's: Chapter 2 duty plus any AFAD (s 231(6)(a)). Where several
-- people buy together, each answer about a person is about every buyer; the two-buyer question covers the case where only
-- one of them qualifies.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties Act 2001 (Qld) -- the buyer's questions`

GIVEN `what I am buying`                         IS A `What is bought`
      `the price`                                IS A NUMBER
      `the property's value`                     IS A NUMBER
      `the value of other property in the purchase` IS A NUMBER
      `I am buying as an individual`             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I am entitled to possession`      IS A DATE
      `I will live there`                        IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I start living there`             IS A DATE
      `my residency`                             IS A `Residency`
      `I am at least 18`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have never held other residential land` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have never had a vacant land concession` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the home is new`                          IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Home purchase`
`my purchase from my answers` `what I am buying` `the price` `the property's value` `the value of other property in the purchase` `I am buying as an individual` `the day I am entitled to possession` `I will live there` `the day I start living there` `my residency` `I am at least 18` `I have never held other residential land` `I have never had a vacant land concession` `the home is new` MEANS
    `Home purchase` WITH
        `what is bought`                                    IS `what I am buying`
        `consideration`                                     IS `the price`
        `unencumbered value`                                IS `the property's value`
        `value of the other dutiable property`              IS `the value of other property in the purchase`
        `the transferees are individuals and not trustees`  IS `I am buying as an individual`
        `transfer date`                                     IS `the day I am entitled to possession`
        `the transferees will occupy it as their principal place of residence` IS `I will live there`
        `occupation date`                                   IS `the day I start living there`
        `residency of the transferees`                      IS `my residency`
        `the transferees are at least 18 on the day liability arises` IS `I am at least 18`
        `the transferees never held an interest in other residential land` IS `I have never held other residential land`
        `the transferees were never vacant land concession beneficiaries for other land` IS `I have never had a vacant land concession`
        `the residence is a new home`                       IS `the home is new`

§§ `Transfer duty on buying a home or a block of land`

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, what is the dutiable value of my purchase of land: the greater of the price and the property's unencumbered value (s 11(7))?
GIVEN `the price`            IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller you take over (s 12); 0 if there is no price
      `the property's value` IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of what you are buying, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); for an arm's-length sale at market price, the price
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my purchase` IS
    `the dutiable value given` `the price` `and` `the property's value`

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, how much transfer duty would I pay at the general rate, with no home concession (s 24(2), Schedule 3)?
GIVEN `the price`            IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller you take over (s 12); 0 if there is no price
      `the property's value` IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of what you are buying, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); for an arm's-length sale at market price, the price
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much transfer duty would I pay at the general rate` IS
    `the general rate applied to` (`the dutiable value given` `the price` `and` `the property's value`)

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, which home concession does my purchase get: the home, first home, first home and new home, or first home vacant land concession (ss 86-92B)?
GIVEN `what I am buying`                         IS A `What is bought` @desc What you are buying. One of: "residential land" (land with a house, unit or other residence on it, with its yard); "vacant land" (land with no building on it when you buy, on which a home is to be built); "other dutiable property"
      `the price`                                IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller you take over (s 12); 0 if there is no price
      `the property's value`                     IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of what you are buying, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); for an arm's-length sale at market price, the price
      `the value of other property in the purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that value is for things other than the home (or block) and its yard, such as furniture and other goods, or land not used with the home, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `I am buying as an individual`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are buying as an individual in your own right, not as a trustee and not as a company
      `the day I am entitled to possession`      IS A DATE @desc The day you become entitled to possession of the land under the contract (usually the settlement date)
      `I will live there`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, will live there (for vacant land, in the home to be built) as your principal place of residence, as owner
      `the day I start living there`             IS A DATE @desc The day you start, or will start, living there as your principal place of residence (any date if you will not live there)
      `my residency`                             IS A `Residency` @desc Your status on the day you sign the contract, and every other buyer's. One of: "an Australian citizen"; "the holder of a permanent visa"; "a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa"; "the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa"; "an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa" (a parent visa applicant who applied before 8 May 2018 is "none of these"); "none of these"
      `I am at least 18`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are at least 18 years old on the day you sign the contract
      `I have never held other residential land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never held an interest in any other residential land, in Queensland or anywhere else (ignore interests held only as a trustee, as a tenant or as a mortgagee)
      `I have never had a vacant land concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never had the first home vacant land concession for other land
      `the home is new`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has never been lived in or sold as a place of residence, or is a substantially renovated home sold as new residential premises for GST
GIVETH A `Home concession`
DECIDE `Which home concession do I get` IS
    `the home concession for` (`my purchase from my answers` `what I am buying` `the price` `the property's value` `the value of other property in the purchase` `I am buying as an individual` `the day I am entitled to possession` `I will live there` `the day I start living there` `my residency` `I am at least 18` `I have never held other residential land` `I have never had a vacant land concession` `the home is new`)

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, how much transfer duty under Chapter 2 must I pay on buying my home or a block of land, with any home concession I get, before any additional foreign acquirer duty (ss 24, 91, 92, 92A, 92B)? A foreign buyer also pays AFAD, which the Act counts as part of transfer duty (s 231(6)(a)); the question on how much transfer duty I must pay gives the total
GIVEN `what I am buying`                         IS A `What is bought` @desc What you are buying. One of: "residential land" (land with a house, unit or other residence on it, with its yard); "vacant land" (land with no building on it when you buy, on which a home is to be built); "other dutiable property"
      `the price`                                IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller you take over (s 12); 0 if there is no price
      `the property's value`                     IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of what you are buying, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); for an arm's-length sale at market price, the price
      `the value of other property in the purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that value is for things other than the home (or block) and its yard, such as furniture and other goods, or land not used with the home, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `I am buying as an individual`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are buying as an individual in your own right, not as a trustee and not as a company
      `the day I am entitled to possession`      IS A DATE @desc The day you become entitled to possession of the land under the contract (usually the settlement date)
      `I will live there`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, will live there (for vacant land, in the home to be built) as your principal place of residence, as owner
      `the day I start living there`             IS A DATE @desc The day you start, or will start, living there as your principal place of residence (any date if you will not live there)
      `my residency`                             IS A `Residency` @desc Your status on the day you sign the contract, and every other buyer's. One of: "an Australian citizen"; "the holder of a permanent visa"; "a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa"; "the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa"; "an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa" (a parent visa applicant who applied before 8 May 2018 is "none of these"); "none of these"
      `I am at least 18`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are at least 18 years old on the day you sign the contract
      `I have never held other residential land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never held an interest in any other residential land, in Queensland or anywhere else (ignore interests held only as a trustee, as a tenant or as a mortgagee)
      `I have never had a vacant land concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never had the first home vacant land concession for other land
      `the home is new`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has never been lived in or sold as a place of residence, or is a substantially renovated home sold as new residential premises for GST
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much transfer duty must I pay before AFAD` IS
    `the transfer duty answer for` (`my purchase from my answers` `what I am buying` `the price` `the property's value` `the value of other property in the purchase` `I am buying as an individual` `the day I am entitled to possession` `I will live there` `the day I start living there` `my residency` `I am at least 18` `I have never held other residential land` `I have never had a vacant land concession` `the home is new`)

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, how much transfer duty must I pay in all on buying my home or a block of land: the Chapter 2 duty with any home concession I get, plus any additional foreign acquirer duty (AFAD) if we are foreign buyers, which the Act counts as transfer duty (ss 24, 91-92B, 231(5), (6)(a), 240, 243, 244)?
GIVEN `what I am buying`                         IS A `What is bought` @desc What you are buying. One of: "residential land" (land with a house, unit or other residence on it, with its yard); "vacant land" (land with no building on it when you buy, on which a home is to be built); "other dutiable property"
      `the price`                                IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller you take over (s 12); 0 if there is no price
      `the property's value`                     IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of what you are buying, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); for an arm's-length sale at market price, the price
      `the value of other property in the purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that value is for things other than the home (or block) and its yard, such as furniture and other goods, or land not used with the home, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `I am buying as an individual`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are buying as an individual in your own right, not as a trustee and not as a company
      `the day I am entitled to possession`      IS A DATE @desc The day you become entitled to possession of the land under the contract (usually the settlement date)
      `I will live there`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, will live there (for vacant land, in the home to be built) as your principal place of residence, as owner
      `the day I start living there`             IS A DATE @desc The day you start, or will start, living there as your principal place of residence (any date if you will not live there)
      `my residency`                             IS A `Residency` @desc Your status on the day you sign the contract, and every other buyer's. One of: "an Australian citizen"; "the holder of a permanent visa"; "a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa"; "the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa"; "an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa" (a parent visa applicant who applied before 8 May 2018 is "none of these"); "none of these"
      `I am at least 18`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are at least 18 years old on the day you sign the contract
      `I have never held other residential land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never held an interest in any other residential land, in Queensland or anywhere else (ignore interests held only as a trustee, as a tenant or as a mortgagee)
      `I have never had a vacant land concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never had the first home vacant land concession for other land
      `the home is new`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has never been lived in or sold as a place of residence, or is a substantially renovated home sold as new residential premises for GST
      `the land is residential`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only matters if you are not an Australian citizen or permanent resident: whether the land is used, or will be used, solely or mainly for residential purposes, with a house, unit or other single-family dwelling on it or to be built or made on it (AFAD residential land, s 232)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much transfer duty must I pay` IS
    `the transfer duty including any AFAD on` (`my purchase from my answers` `what I am buying` `the price` `the property's value` `the value of other property in the purchase` `I am buying as an individual` `the day I am entitled to possession` `I will live there` `the day I start living there` `my residency` `I am at least 18` `I have never held other residential land` `I have never had a vacant land concession` `the home is new`) `the land is residential`

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, how much transfer duty does my home concession save me, compared with the general rate (ss 91, 92, 92A, 92B)?
GIVEN `what I am buying`                         IS A `What is bought` @desc What you are buying. One of: "residential land" (land with a house, unit or other residence on it, with its yard); "vacant land" (land with no building on it when you buy, on which a home is to be built); "other dutiable property"
      `the price`                                IS A NUMBER @desc The price you are paying, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller you take over (s 12); 0 if there is no price
      `the property's value`                     IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of what you are buying, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); for an arm's-length sale at market price, the price
      `the value of other property in the purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that value is for things other than the home (or block) and its yard, such as furniture and other goods, or land not used with the home, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `I am buying as an individual`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are buying as an individual in your own right, not as a trustee and not as a company
      `the day I am entitled to possession`      IS A DATE @desc The day you become entitled to possession of the land under the contract (usually the settlement date)
      `I will live there`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, will live there (for vacant land, in the home to be built) as your principal place of residence, as owner
      `the day I start living there`             IS A DATE @desc The day you start, or will start, living there as your principal place of residence (any date if you will not live there)
      `my residency`                             IS A `Residency` @desc Your status on the day you sign the contract, and every other buyer's. One of: "an Australian citizen"; "the holder of a permanent visa"; "a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa"; "the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa"; "an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa" (a parent visa applicant who applied before 8 May 2018 is "none of these"); "none of these"
      `I am at least 18`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, are at least 18 years old on the day you sign the contract
      `I have never held other residential land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never held an interest in any other residential land, in Queensland or anywhere else (ignore interests held only as a trustee, as a tenant or as a mortgagee)
      `I have never had a vacant land concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, and every other buyer, have never had the first home vacant land concession for other land
      `the home is new`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has never been lived in or sold as a place of residence, or is a substantially renovated home sold as new residential premises for GST
GIVETH A `Saving answer`
DECIDE `How much does my home concession save me` IS
    `the saving answer for` (`my purchase from my answers` `what I am buying` `the price` `the property's value` `the value of other property in the purchase` `I am buying as an individual` `the day I am entitled to possession` `I will live there` `the day I start living there` `my residency` `I am at least 18` `I have never held other residential land` `I have never had a vacant land concession` `the home is new`)

-- Situation: two people buy together and only one of them will have it as a home (the other will not live there, or is
-- not a citizen, permanent resident or specified foreign retiree), or, for vacant land, as a first home. The person
-- answers are about the one who will.
@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, we are two buyers and only one of us will have the home as a home or first home: how much transfer duty under Chapter 2 is payable, before any additional foreign acquirer duty on a foreign buyer's share (s 93(1)(c)(ii), (7))?
GIVEN `what I am buying`                         IS A `What is bought` @desc What you are buying. One of: "residential land" (land with a house, unit or other residence on it, with its yard); "vacant land" (land with no building on it when you buy, on which a home is to be built); "other dutiable property"
      `the price`                                IS A NUMBER @desc The price the two of you are paying, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller you take over (s 12); 0 if there is no price
      `the property's value`                     IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of what you are buying, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); for an arm's-length sale at market price, the price
      `the value of other property in the purchase` IS A NUMBER @desc How much of that value is for things other than the home and its yard, such as furniture and other goods, or land not used with the home, in Australian dollars; 0 if none
      `I am buying as an individual`             IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether both of you are buying as individuals in your own right, not as trustees and not as companies
      `the day I am entitled to possession`      IS A DATE @desc The day you become entitled to possession of the land under the contract (usually the settlement date)
      `I will live there`                        IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the buyer who will have it as a home will live there as their principal place of residence, as owner
      `the day I start living there`             IS A DATE @desc The day that buyer starts, or will start, living there as their principal place of residence
      `my residency`                             IS A `Residency` @desc That buyer's status on the day you sign the contract. One of: "an Australian citizen"; "the holder of a permanent visa"; "a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa"; "the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa"; "an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa" (a parent visa applicant who applied before 8 May 2018 is "none of these"); "none of these"
      `I am at least 18`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that buyer is at least 18 years old on the day you sign the contract
      `I have never held other residential land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that buyer has never held an interest in any other residential land, in Queensland or anywhere else (ignore interests held only as a trustee, as a tenant or as a mortgagee)
      `I have never had a vacant land concession` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that buyer has never had the first home vacant land concession for other land
      `the home is new`                          IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the home has never been lived in or sold as a place of residence, or is a substantially renovated home sold as new residential premises for GST
      `the share of the buyer who will live there` IS A NUMBER @desc The share of the buyer who will have it as a home, as a fraction of both buyers' shares (0.5 for half)
      `the other buyer qualifies too`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other buyer qualifies too. For land with a home on it: the other buyer will also live there as their principal place of residence, as owner, within 1 year after the day of possession, and is an Australian citizen, permanent resident or specified foreign retiree. For vacant land: the home to be built will also be the other buyer's first home: they will live in it within 2 years after the day of possession, have never held an interest in residential land or had a vacant land concession for other land, are at least 18, and are an Australian citizen, permanent resident or specified foreign retiree
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much transfer duty do we pay when only one of us qualifies` IS
    `the s 93 answer for` (`Two-buyer purchase` WITH
        `the purchase, with the facts of the buyer who will live there` IS `my purchase from my answers` `what I am buying` `the price` `the property's value` `the value of other property in the purchase` `I am buying as an individual` `the day I am entitled to possession` `I will live there` `the day I start living there` `my residency` `I am at least 18` `I have never held other residential land` `I have never had a vacant land concession` `the home is new`
        `that buyer's interest` IS `the share of the buyer who will live there`
        `the other buyer qualifies too` IS `the other buyer qualifies too`)

@export Under the Queensland Duties Regulation 2023, if my purchase is settled electronically (an ELN transfer), can my home concession still be applied to it (s 5, Schedule 2 Part 1)?
GIVEN `the home concession` IS A `Home concession` @desc The concession your purchase gets. One of: "no home concession"; "the home concession (s 91)"; "the first home concession (s 92)"; "the first home and new home concession (s 92A)"; "the first home vacant land concession (s 92B)"; "the concession for one of two buyers (s 93)"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can my concession be applied in an electronic transfer` IF
    `the concession is prescribed for ELN transfers and ELN lodgements` `the home concession`

§§ `Lodging and paying the transfer duty`

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, by what day must the contract (or transfer) and the transfer duty form be lodged for duty (ss 16, 19(3), 20, Schedule 2)?
GIVEN `the day liability arose` IS A DATE @desc The day you signed the contract to buy (the agreement for transfer); if there was no contract, the earliest of the day the transfer was signed by the parties, the day the electronic workspace was locked with the signed transfer in it, and the day of the transfer
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must the contract be lodged for duty` IS
    `the last day to lodge, for a liability arising on` `the day liability arose`

@export Under the Queensland Taxation Administration Act 2001, by what day must I pay the transfer duty (s 30(1)(b), (e), (2))?
GIVEN `how my duty is assessed`                  IS A `How the duty is assessed` @desc How your duty is assessed. One of: "by a self assessor lodging a transaction statement" (your lawyer or conveyancer is a registered self assessor and lodges a transaction statement); "by the commissioner giving an assessment notice"
      `the day the transaction statement was lodged` IS A DATE @desc For self assessment, the day the self assessor lodged the transaction statement (any date otherwise)
      `the day the assessment notice was given`  IS A DATE @desc For an assessment notice, the day it was given to you (any date otherwise)
      `the payment date in the notice`           IS A DATE @desc For an assessment notice, the date it states the duty must be paid by (any date otherwise)
GIVETH A `Payment answer`
DECIDE `By when must I pay the transfer duty` IS
    `the s 30 time for payment` `how my duty is assessed` `the day the transaction statement was lodged` `the day the assessment notice was given` `the payment date in the notice`

§§ `If I sell, rent out or do not move in` -- situation: only for a purchase assessed with a home concession

GIVEN `the concession I was assessed with`    IS A `Home concession`
      `the dutiable value of my purchase`     IS A NUMBER
      `the transfer duty I was assessed`      IS A NUMBER
      `I bought vacant land`                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I was entitled to possession`  IS A DATE
      `I have moved in`                       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I moved in`                    IS A DATE
      `what I did with the property`          IS A `Dealing`
      `the day I did it`                      IS A DATE
      `it happened because of an intervening event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `today`                                 IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Concession follow-up`
`my follow-up from my answers` `the concession I was assessed with` `the dutiable value of my purchase` `the transfer duty I was assessed` `I bought vacant land` `the day I was entitled to possession` `I have moved in` `the day I moved in` `what I did with the property` `the day I did it` `it happened because of an intervening event` `today` MEANS
    `Concession follow-up` WITH
        `the concession assessed`                   IS `the concession I was assessed with`
        `the dutiable value of the transaction`     IS `the dutiable value of my purchase`
        `the transfer duty assessed`                IS `the transfer duty I was assessed`
        `the land is vacant land`                   IS `I bought vacant land`
        `the transferee's transfer date`            IS `the day I was entitled to possession`
        `the transferee has occupied the residence` IS `I have moved in`
        `the transferee's occupation date`          IS `the day I moved in`
        `the dealing`                               IS `what I did with the property`
        `the date of the dealing`                   IS `the day I did it`
        `it was because of an intervening event`    IS `it happened because of an intervening event`
        `the day asked about`                       IS `today`

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, I got a home concession: if I sell or rent out the home within a year of moving in, or do not move in in time, what happens (ss 153, 154)?
GIVEN `the concession I was assessed with`    IS A `Home concession` @desc The concession your transfer duty was assessed with. One of: "no home concession"; "the home concession (s 91)"; "the first home concession (s 92)"; "the first home and new home concession (s 92A)"; "the first home vacant land concession (s 92B)"; "the concession for one of two buyers (s 93)"
      `the dutiable value of my purchase`     IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of your purchase, in Australian dollars (the greater of the price and the unencumbered value)
      `the transfer duty I was assessed`      IS A NUMBER @desc The transfer duty you were assessed with the concession, in Australian dollars
      `I bought vacant land`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought vacant land to build your first home on (otherwise land with a home on it)
      `the day I was entitled to possession`  IS A DATE @desc The day you became entitled to possession of the land under the contract (usually settlement)
      `I have moved in`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have started living there as your principal place of residence
      `the day I moved in`                    IS A DATE @desc The day you started living there as your principal place of residence (any date if you have not)
      `what I did with the property`          IS A `Dealing` @desc What you did. One of: "no dealing with the land"; "a transfer of part or all of the land" (sold or gave away part or all of it); "a lease or other grant of exclusive possession of all of the land, or of part of it other than for residential purposes"; "a residential lease of part, but not all, of the land" (for example letting a room or a granny flat); "a transfer of part of the land to the transferee's spouse that is exempt under s 151"
      `the day I did it`                      IS A DATE @desc The day of that transfer, lease or grant of possession (any date if none)
      `it happened because of an intervening event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened, or you could not move in, because of a natural disaster such as fire or flood, or because of a death or incapacity
      `today`                                 IS A DATE @desc Today's date, to tell whether the time to move in has passed
GIVETH A `Clawback answer`
DECIDE `What happens to my concession if I sell, rent out or do not move in` IS
    `the reassessment for` (`my follow-up from my answers` `the concession I was assessed with` `the dutiable value of my purchase` `the transfer duty I was assessed` `I bought vacant land` `the day I was entitled to possession` `I have moved in` `the day I moved in` `what I did with the property` `the day I did it` `it happened because of an intervening event` `today`)

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, I got a home concession: by what day must I tell the Commissioner that I sold, leased or did not move in, and lodge the documents for reassessment (s 155)?
GIVEN `the concession I was assessed with`    IS A `Home concession` @desc The concession your transfer duty was assessed with. One of: "no home concession"; "the home concession (s 91)"; "the first home concession (s 92)"; "the first home and new home concession (s 92A)"; "the first home vacant land concession (s 92B)"; "the concession for one of two buyers (s 93)"
      `the dutiable value of my purchase`     IS A NUMBER @desc The dutiable value of your purchase, in Australian dollars (the greater of the price and the unencumbered value)
      `the transfer duty I was assessed`      IS A NUMBER @desc The transfer duty you were assessed with the concession, in Australian dollars
      `I bought vacant land`                  IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you bought vacant land to build your first home on (otherwise land with a home on it)
      `the day I was entitled to possession`  IS A DATE @desc The day you became entitled to possession of the land under the contract (usually settlement)
      `I have moved in`                       IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have started living there as your principal place of residence
      `the day I moved in`                    IS A DATE @desc The day you started living there as your principal place of residence (any date if you have not)
      `what I did with the property`          IS A `Dealing` @desc What you did. One of: "no dealing with the land"; "a transfer of part or all of the land" (sold or gave away part or all of it); "a lease or other grant of exclusive possession of all of the land, or of part of it other than for residential purposes"; "a residential lease of part, but not all, of the land" (for example letting a room or a granny flat); "a transfer of part of the land to the transferee's spouse that is exempt under s 151"
      `the day I did it`                      IS A DATE @desc The day of that transfer, lease or grant of possession (any date if none)
      `it happened because of an intervening event` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it happened, or you could not move in, because of a natural disaster such as fire or flood, or because of a death or incapacity
      `today`                                 IS A DATE @desc Today's date, to tell whether the time to move in has passed
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
DECIDE `By when must I tell the Commissioner` IS
    `the notice due for` (`my follow-up from my answers` `the concession I was assessed with` `the dutiable value of my purchase` `the transfer duty I was assessed` `I bought vacant land` `the day I was entitled to possession` `I have moved in` `the day I moved in` `what I did with the property` `the day I did it` `it happened because of an intervening event` `today`)

§§ `Additional foreign acquirer duty` -- situation: only if a buyer is not an Australian citizen or permanent resident

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, am I a foreign individual for additional foreign acquirer duty (s 235)?
GIVEN `my residency` IS A `Residency` @desc Your status on the day you sign the contract. One of: "an Australian citizen"; "the holder of a permanent visa"; "a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa"; "the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa"; "an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa" (a parent visa applicant who applied before 8 May 2018 is "none of these"); "none of these"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I a foreign individual` IF
    `is a foreign individual` `my residency`

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, how much additional foreign acquirer duty (AFAD, 8%) must I pay on buying residential land? It is added to the Chapter 2 transfer duty and is itself part of transfer duty (s 231(5), (6)(a)), and no home concession reduces it (ss 240, 243, 244)
GIVEN `the price`            IS A NUMBER @desc The price being paid for the land and its home, all of it and not only your share, in Australian dollars, including any debts or liabilities of the seller taken over (s 12); leave out furniture and other goods bought with it, which are not AFAD residential land
      `the property's value` IS A NUMBER @desc The market value of the land and its home, all of it and not only your share, in Australian dollars, ignoring any mortgage or other encumbrance (its unencumbered value, s 14); leave out furniture and other goods
      `my share`             IS A NUMBER @desc Your share of what is bought, as a fraction of all the buyers' shares (1 if you are the only buyer, 0.5 for half)
      `my residency`         IS A `Residency` @desc Your status on the day you sign the contract. One of: "an Australian citizen"; "the holder of a permanent visa"; "a New Zealand citizen holding a special category visa"; "the holder of a Subclass 405 or 410 retirement visa"; "an undecided Subclass 103 or 143 parent visa applicant who applied on or after 8 May 2018 and whose last substantive visa was a Subclass 405 or 410 visa" (a parent visa applicant who applied before 8 May 2018 is "none of these"); "none of these"
      `the land is residential` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the land is used, or will be used, solely or mainly for residential purposes, with a house, unit or other single-family dwelling on it or to be built or made on it (AFAD residential land, s 232)
GIVETH A `Duty answer`
DECIDE `How much additional foreign acquirer duty must I pay` IS
    `the AFAD answer for` (`the dutiable value given` `the price` `and` `the property's value`) `my share` `my residency` `the land is residential`

§§ `If I pay late, or the duty is reassessed` -- situation: only if the duty was not paid by the due date, or a reassessment or default assessment is made

@export Under the Queensland Taxation Administration Act 2001, from what day does unpaid tax interest run on my duty (s 54(5), (6))?
GIVEN `the due date`                     IS A DATE @desc The date by which the duty had to be paid (for a reassessment, the due date of the original assessment)
      `the day the documents had to be lodged` IS A DATE @desc The last day for lodging the documents for the assessment (for transfer duty, 30 days after you signed the contract)
      `the day I lodged them`            IS A DATE @desc The day you lodged them
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From what day does unpaid tax interest run` IS
    `the start date for unpaid tax interest` `the due date` (`the days of noncompliance from` `the day the documents had to be lodged` `to` `the day I lodged them`)

@export Under the Queensland Taxation Administration Act 2001, how much unpaid tax interest will I owe on duty I have not paid (s 54(2))?
GIVEN `the unpaid duty`          IS A NUMBER @desc The duty still unpaid, in Australian dollars
      `the prescribed rate`      IS A NUMBER @desc The prescribed rate of interest a year, as a decimal (0.10 for 10%), set by the Taxation Administration Regulation 2022, which this encoding does not hold
      `the start date`           IS A DATE @desc The day interest starts to run (see the question on when unpaid tax interest runs)
      `the day I pay in full`    IS A DATE @desc The day you pay the duty in full
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much unpaid tax interest will I owe` IS
    `the unpaid tax interest on` `the unpaid duty` `at` `the prescribed rate` `from` `the start date` `to` `the day I pay in full`

@export Under the Queensland Taxation Administration Act 2001, what penalty tax can I be charged on a default assessment or on a reassessment that increases my duty, before any remission (s 58)?
GIVEN `it is a default assessment`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the assessment is a default assessment because you did not lodge or give what was required, or the commissioner was not satisfied with it (s 13(1)(a) or (b)), or a reassessment of such an assessment
      `the duty now assessed`                   IS A NUMBER @desc The duty on that default assessment, or on the latest reassessment, in Australian dollars
      `the duty on the original assessment`     IS A NUMBER @desc The duty on the first assessment, in Australian dollars
      `the lowest duty on an earlier reassessment` IS A NUMBER @desc The lowest duty on any earlier reassessment, in Australian dollars (the original amount if there was none)
      `the commissioner finds I did not report or hindered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the commissioner is satisfied that you did not tell the commissioner within 30 days that your assessment was too low (s 28), or hindered the commissioner from learning of your liability
GIVETH A `Penalty tax`
DECIDE `What penalty tax can I be charged` IS
    `the penalty tax for` `it is a default assessment` `the duty now assessed` `the duty on the original assessment` `the lowest duty on an earlier reassessment` `the commissioner finds I did not report or hindered`

§§ `If I disagree with the assessment` -- situation: only if the buyer is dissatisfied with an assessment or reassessment

@export Under the Queensland Taxation Administration Act 2001, by what day must I lodge an objection to my duty assessment (ss 63, 65)?
GIVEN `the day the assessment notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the assessment notice (or the reassessment notice) was given to you
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I object` IS
    `the last day to object to an assessment notice given on` `the day the assessment notice was given`

@export Under the Queensland Taxation Administration Act 2001, after the Commissioner decides my objection, can I appeal to the Supreme Court or apply to QCAT for review, and by when (s 69)?
GIVEN `the day the decision notice was given` IS A DATE @desc The day the commissioner's written notice of the decision on your objection was given to you
      `I have paid in full`                   IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have paid the whole of the duty and late payment interest under the assessment
GIVETH A `Appeal answer`
DECIDE `Can I appeal or seek review, and by when` IS
    `the s 69 right of appeal or review` `the day the decision notice was given` `I have paid in full`

§§ `Registering or transferring a vehicle`

GIVEN `my application`                         IS A `Vehicle application`
      `registered before`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has a list price`                    IS A BOOLEAN
      `its list price`                         IS A NUMBER
      `options not in the list price`          IS A NUMBER
      `what I pay for it`                      IS A NUMBER
      `its market value`                       IS A NUMBER
      `it is modified for a person with a disability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the modifications`         IS A NUMBER
      `its engine`                             IS A `Kind of vehicle`
      `its GVM is more than 4.5t`              IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a special vehicle`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am an ex-serviceperson with concessional registration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a motorised wheelchair`           IS A BOOLEAN
      `I lost the use of a leg and need it for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I lost the use of a leg and need it for education for work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a gift`                           IS A BOOLEAN
      `my relationship to the registered operator` IS A `Relationship to the registered operator`
GIVETH A `Vehicle application facts`
`my vehicle application from my answers` `my application` `registered before` `it has a list price` `its list price` `options not in the list price` `what I pay for it` `its market value` `it is modified for a person with a disability` `the value of the modifications` `its engine` `its GVM is more than 4.5t` `it is a special vehicle` `I am an ex-serviceperson with concessional registration` `it is a motorised wheelchair` `I lost the use of a leg and need it for work` `I lost the use of a leg and need it for education for work` `it is a gift` `my relationship to the registered operator` MEANS
    `Vehicle application facts` WITH
        `the application`                                   IS `my application`
        `the vehicle has been registered before, in Queensland or another State` IS `registered before`
        `the vehicle has a list price`                      IS `it has a list price`
        `the list price`                                    IS `its list price`
        `optional equipment not included in the list price` IS `options not in the list price`
        `the total consideration`                           IS `what I pay for it`
        `the market value`                                  IS `its market value`
        `the vehicle is modified for a person with a disability` IS `it is modified for a person with a disability`
        `the value of the modifications`                    IS `the value of the modifications`
        `the kind of vehicle`                               IS `its engine`
        `the vehicle has a GVM of more than 4.5t`           IS `its GVM is more than 4.5t`
        `the vehicle is a special vehicle`                  IS `it is a special vehicle`
        `the applicant is an ex-serviceperson entitled to concessional registration fees for the vehicle` IS `I am an ex-serviceperson with concessional registration`
        `the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair for a disabled person's use` IS `it is a motorised wheelchair`
        `the applicant has lost the use of a leg, and the vehicle is for travel to and from work because they cannot use public transport` IS `I lost the use of a leg and need it for work`
        `the applicant has lost the use of a leg, and the vehicle is for travel to and from education for getting work because they cannot use public transport` IS `I lost the use of a leg and need it for education for work`
        `the transfer is wholly by way of gift`             IS `it is a gift`
        `the transferee's relationship to the registered operator` IS `my relationship to the registered operator`

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, how much vehicle registration duty must I pay to register a vehicle, or to have one transferred into my name, and am I exempt (ss 377-383, 390, Schedule 4C)?
GIVEN `my application`                         IS A `Vehicle application` @desc What you are applying for. One of: "an application to register the vehicle"; "an application to transfer the vehicle to another person" (a registered vehicle being transferred into your name)
      `registered before`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has been registered before, in Queensland or another State
      `it has a list price`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has a manufacturer's list price
      `its list price`                         IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's list price, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `options not in the list price`          IS A NUMBER @desc The price of all optional equipment not included in the list price, in Australian dollars
      `what I pay for it`                      IS A NUMBER @desc The total price you pay, in Australian dollars, including any deposit, trade-in allowance and optional equipment (0 for a gift)
      `its market value`                       IS A NUMBER @desc What the vehicle might reasonably sell for on the open market, free of encumbrances, in Australian dollars
      `it is modified for a person with a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has been modified so that a person with a disability can drive it or be carried in it, and is applied for by that person, or their relative or carer, for their use
      `the value of the modifications`         IS A NUMBER @desc The value of those modifications, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `its engine`                             IS A `Kind of vehicle` @desc The kind of vehicle. One of: "a hybrid vehicle, with any number of cylinders"; "an electric vehicle"; "a vehicle with 1 to 4 cylinders"; "a vehicle with 2 rotors"; "a steam vehicle"; "a vehicle with 5 or 6 cylinders"; "a vehicle with 3 rotors"; "a vehicle with 7 or more cylinders"; "a vehicle of another kind"
      `its GVM is more than 4.5t`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle's gross vehicle mass (GVM) is more than 4.5 tonnes
      `it is a special vehicle`                IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is a special vehicle: registered, or to be registered, as a special vehicle under the Vehicle Registration Regulation, or mobile machinery not built on a truck chassis
      `I am an ex-serviceperson with concessional registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an ex-serviceperson entitled to concessional registration fees for this vehicle
      `it is a motorised wheelchair`           IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a motorised wheelchair for a disabled person's use
      `I lost the use of a leg and need it for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lost the use of one or both legs and the vehicle is for getting to and from your work because you cannot use public transport
      `I lost the use of a leg and need it for education for work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have lost the use of one or both legs and the vehicle is for getting to and from education undertaken to get work, because you cannot use public transport
      `it is a gift`                           IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a transfer, whether the vehicle (or your interest in it) is being transferred to you wholly as a gift
      `my relationship to the registered operator` IS A `Relationship to the registered operator` @desc For a transfer, what you are to the person it is registered to. One of: "the registered operator's spouse"; "a parent or grandparent of the registered operator"; "a parent or grandparent of the registered operator's spouse"; "a child, stepchild or grandchild of the registered operator"; "a child, stepchild or grandchild of the registered operator's spouse"; "the spouse of a parent, grandparent, child, stepchild or grandchild of the registered operator or of their spouse"; "none of these"
GIVETH A `Vehicle duty answer`
DECIDE `How much vehicle registration duty must I pay` IS
    `the vehicle registration duty answer for` (`my vehicle application from my answers` `my application` `registered before` `it has a list price` `its list price` `options not in the list price` `what I pay for it` `its market value` `it is modified for a person with a disability` `the value of the modifications` `its engine` `its GVM is more than 4.5t` `it is a special vehicle` `I am an ex-serviceperson with concessional registration` `it is a motorised wheelchair` `I lost the use of a leg and need it for work` `I lost the use of a leg and need it for education for work` `it is a gift` `my relationship to the registered operator`)

@export Under the Queensland Duties Act 2001, what is the dutiable value of the vehicle I am registering or having transferred to me (s 378)?
GIVEN `my application`                         IS A `Vehicle application` @desc What you are applying for. One of: "an application to register the vehicle"; "an application to transfer the vehicle to another person" (a registered vehicle being transferred into your name)
      `registered before`                      IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has been registered before, in Queensland or another State
      `it has a list price`                    IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has a manufacturer's list price
      `its list price`                         IS A NUMBER @desc The vehicle's list price, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
      `options not in the list price`          IS A NUMBER @desc The price of all optional equipment not included in the list price, in Australian dollars
      `what I pay for it`                      IS A NUMBER @desc The total price you pay, in Australian dollars, including any deposit, trade-in allowance and optional equipment (0 for a gift)
      `its market value`                       IS A NUMBER @desc What the vehicle might reasonably sell for on the open market, free of encumbrances, in Australian dollars
      `it is modified for a person with a disability` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle has been modified so that a person with a disability can drive it or be carried in it, and is applied for by that person, or their relative or carer, for their use
      `the value of the modifications`         IS A NUMBER @desc The value of those modifications, in Australian dollars (0 if none)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the dutiable value of my vehicle` IS
    -- The fields after `the value of the modifications` are not read by s 378: fixed placeholders.
    `the dutiable value of the vehicle in` (`my vehicle application from my answers` `my application` `registered before` `it has a list price` `its list price` `options not in the list price` `what I pay for it` `its market value` `it is modified for a person with a disability` `the value of the modifications` `a vehicle of another kind` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `none of these`)
